From 282e79c340080088810e708a454eb9f08d036d71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Correa da Silva Sanches <juca@members.fsf.org>
Date: Sat, 14 Mar 2026 13:13:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/25] Tone generator: pitch control, release envelope, linear
 interpolation; fix FDC dskchg polarity

Tone generator improvements:
- Expand voice register array from 28 to 32 (fixes dropped group 0xA writes)
- Add pitch control from group 1 registers (reg[4] as 16-bit pitch increment)
- Add 50ms release envelope on key-off for smooth fade-out
- Add 2-second hold timer for voice status readback (firmware compatibility)
- Add linear interpolation between samples for smoother playback
- Resolve waveform on register strobe (group 0, bank 2 with bit 15 set)
- Trigger param updates on pitch (group 1) and pan (group 4) register writes
- Fix pan direction (L/R were swapped)
- Use IC307 exclusively for waveform lookup (only dumped ROM chip)

FDC fix: invert dskchg_r() for active-low hardware signal. The firmware
checks Port D bit 6 before issuing any FDC commands and was seeing "no disk"
because MAME's dskchg_r() is active-high while the hardware expects active-low.
